    "notes": "Deductive Order - Organizing info with main ideas and recommendations first.\nChronological Order - Arranging information in time sequence.\nGeographical Order - Organizing data based on physical location.\nDirect Approach - Presenting the most important information immediately.\nData Organization - Structuring research results for reports and presentations.",
