    "explanation": "Ask questions to clarify what someone else is saying. If you don't know much about the topic at hand, you might feel that you have very little to contribute. But, one way to participate even if you're not an expert in the subject is to use a questioning technique to clarify what someone else is saying. You might ask a question that rephrases or builds on another person's statement. You shouldn't bring up another topic that you know more about—it's important to remember the purpose of the discussion. Although the people who know the most (or have the most experience) naturally tend to lead the conversation, that doesn't mean you should completely check out. Focus on paying attention so that you can ask clarifying questions when appropriate. You may be eager to contribute, but that doesn't mean you should voice an uninformed opinion. You might say something inaccurate, which wouldn't help the overall purpose of your conversation.",
